.TH "SECURE\-TERMINAL\-REVIEW" "1" "January 2020" "secure-terminal" "secure-terminal Manual"
.SH "NAME"
\fBsecure\-terminal\-review\fR \- show the review popup by itself
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBsecure\-terminal\-review\fR [\fB\-\-kind\fR paste|copy|clipboard] [\fB\-\-text\fR TEXT] [\fB\-\-theme\fR THEME] [\fB\-\-delay\fR SECONDS]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
secure\-terminal\-review shows the secure\-terminal review popup on its own, with no terminal, tab or pseudo\-terminal behind it\. It hosts the SAME review widget the docked review bar (in the terminal window) and the clipboard sanitizer use, so the transforms, the fully\-revealed per\-character view, the content\-driven Deliver gate and the direction wording are all identical \-\- this is only a separate frame for that one widget\.
.P
The payload to review is \fB\-\-text\fR if given, otherwise text piped on standard input, otherwise a small built\-in sample that contains hidden characters so the bar has something to reveal\. The payload is reviewed exactly as supplied; nothing is stripped\.
.P
On Deliver, the exact delivered text (the box contents plus the neutralized tail) is written to standard output with no added newline \-\- the bytes that would cross\. On Reject, nothing is written to standard output and a \fBrejected\fR notice is written to standard error, so delivering the literal text \fBrejected\fR is never confused with a rejection\.
.P
It needs a running graphical session (a Wayland or X display), like the terminal itself\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-kind\fR paste|copy|clipboard
The review direction, which sets the button wording and the accept note\. Default: paste\.
.TP
\fB\-\-text\fR TEXT
The text to review\. Overrides standard input and the built\-in sample\.
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR THEME
The colour theme of the preview panes\. Default: the configured theme\.
.TP
\fB\-\-delay\fR SECONDS
The anti\-fat\-finger countdown that gates Deliver, in seconds\. Default: 0\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Exits with the Qt application's exit code (0 on a normal close)\.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBsecure\-terminal\fR(1)
